### ============================================
### 8. CHANGE PASSWORD TESTS (Authenticated)
### ============================================

### 8.1 ✅ Login First to Get Token
# @name loginForPasswordChange
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{user1Email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@changePasswordToken = {{loginForPasswordChange.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8.2 ✅ Change Password Successfully
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{changePasswordToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "UpdatedPass123!@#"
}

### 8.3 ❌ Change Password with Wrong Current Password (Should Fail - 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{changePasswordToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "currentPassword": "WrongPassword123",
  "newPassword": "UpdatedPass123!@#"
}

### 8.4 ❌ Change Password with Weak New Password (Should Fail - 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{changePasswordToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "12345"
}

### 8.5 ❌ Change Password Without Token (Should Fail - 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "UpdatedPass123!@#"
}

### 8.6 ✅ Login with Updated Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{user1Email}}",
  "password": "UpdatedPass123!@#"
}

### ============================================
### 9. CONCURRENT SESSION TESTS
### ============================================

### 9.1 ✅ Login from Multiple Devices (User 1)
# @name device1Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{user1Email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@device1Token = {{device1Login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9.2 ✅ Login from Device 2 (User 1)
# @name device2Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{user1Email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@device2Token = {{device2Login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9.3 ✅ Both Devices Access Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{device1Token}}
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{device2Token}}

### 9.4 ✅ Logout from Device 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{device1Token}}

### 9.5 ❌ Device 1 Token Should Be Invalid After Logout
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{device1Token}}

### 9.6 ✅ Device 2 Should Still Work
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{device2Token}}

